In the given code, 'RET' is a shorthand for the function's return value for last executed function only. We're currently only tracking assertions for ArrayList.Insert(), ArrayList.Padd() and ArrayList.Search(). For other functions, use 'OLD(<variable_name>)' to refer to the value of the variable before the function executes and 'RET' to refer to the function's return value for last executed function only.

It's also important to note that C# does not allow to directly read assertion statement into code. It always appears in comments. Hence, this script outputs assertion statements directly.--------------------
